  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the presence of a sure outcome and prefers the lottery without one. The individual explicitly mentions the sure loss in Lottery A and uses this as a key reason to reject it, favoring Lottery B because it offers a chance to avoid any loss. The information considered by the individual (presence of a sure outcome in A) matches the information relevant to the decision reason. Furthermore, the individual’s justification—avoiding the sure loss—aligns with the rule of the decision reason, which prefers the lottery without a sure outcome. Therefore, both the informational basis and the decision rule match closely. The verbal report strongly indicates the use of the decision reason.",
